{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1385900-looking-for-a-particular-requiem-hack","id":1385900,"title":"Looking For a Particular Requiem Hack","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-05T12:45:16-07:00","id":1385900,"title":"Looking For a Particular Requiem Hack","content":"Quite a few years ago, someone posted on this forum (I think it was on this forum, anyway) a hack for Requiem. The main gist of it (or what I remember anyway) was that vampires couldn't purchase Attribute dots with Experiences, due their status as static immortals, and the only way to increase them was through Disciplines (one was linked with each Attribute). I found myself thinking about this hack the other day, and wanted to read over it again, but for the life of me I can't recall any key terms to use in a search, or the name of the person who posted it. Does anyone have any idea as to what I'm referring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T15:21:02-07:00","id":1385949,"title":"","content":"It used to be you couldn\u2019t raise an Attribute or Skill above 5 unless it was through disciplines (which were temporary) until you raised your Blood Potency to 6+ with your new Attribute or Skill cap being whatever your Blood Potency is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T17:34:12-07:00","id":1385979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1385900-looking-for-a-particular-requiem-hack?p=1385949#post1385949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It used to be you couldn\u2019t raise an Attribute or Skill above 5 unless it was through disciplines (which were temporary) until you raised your Blood Potency to 6+ with your new Attribute or Skill cap being whatever your Blood Potency is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but in this rules hack, vampires couldn't raise their Attributes after character creation at all; instead, Disciplines were added to dice pools that involved their linked Attribute. There may have been some other things as well (maybe importing some bits from Masquerade), but that's the salient part for me, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}